  "strategy": "assembly-group",
  "note": "Subsystems are matched by CAD ASSEMBLY-GROUP name, not by leaf node number. The Blender export preserves the CAD hierarchy, so every part of a subsystem sits under a stable group node (e.g. 'Motor Mount', 'SIYI Camera v1'). Leaf names (BodyN.MMM) are auto-generated and get RENUMBERED on every CAD re-export - the previous leaf-keyed map silently mis-assigned 26 parts when this model was rebuilt. Matching on group names survives re-export. lib/vehicle/subsystemLookup.ts walks a mesh's ancestor chain and takes the NEAREST matching group, so nested groups (e.g. 'Board_Frame' inside 'Jetson_OrinNano_simplified') resolve correctly.",
  "nameNormalization": "GLTFLoader rewrites names on load: it strips [ ] . : / (PropertyBinding.sanitizeNodeName) and appends _1/_2/... to disambiguate collisions (createUniqueName). Blender also adds '.001' duplicate suffixes and ':N' instance suffixes, which become trailing digits once the punctuation is stripped ('Motor Mount.001' -> 'Motor Mount001'). subsystemLookup therefore tries an exact match first, then strips trailing digits one at a time. Exact-first matters: 'Component733' is a real group name that must not be truncated to 'Component7'.",
